cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "NMAViz: reading the evidence structure of a network meta-analysis"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sofi-Mahmudi
    given-names: Ahmad
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6829-0823"
repository-code: "https://github.com/choxos/NMAViz"
url: "https://nmaviz.xera.ac"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  NMAViz fits the frequentist graph-theoretical network meta-analysis model in
  the browser and draws the same fitted model through the readings the methods
  literature has proposed for it: an arrangement whose distances are standard
  errors, a bipartite treatment-trial graph, the flow of evidence for one
  comparison, contribution matrices under two methods, a signed study-level
  reconstruction of the estimate, a Hodge decomposition of inconsistency, a
  diffusion, and a system of springs. The engine is checked against the R
  package netmeta on six published networks.
keywords:
  - network meta-analysis
  - evidence synthesis
  - evidence flow
  - hat matrix
  - data visualization
